W:Oft hae i roved by bonnie doon
W:To see the rose and woodbine twine
W:And ilka bird sang o' its love
W:And fondly sae did i o' mine
W:
W:Wi' lightsome heart i pulled a rose
W:Full sweet upon its thorny tree
W:And my false lover stole my rose
W:But ah she left the thorn wi' me
